    pr_ref:  # f3e3
    description: "F69.A1 (blind severity 5/Severe; F72.A1 EXTENSION folded in). The JS analyzer emits imports edges (file->module) and function-to-function calls edges, but NO calls edge from a function body to an imported-module member like fs.readFileSync / http.get. With no call-edge dst to match, the io-boundary catalog has nothing to classify. On injected fixtures, 8 of 9 JS I/O sites (fs.readFileSync/writeFileSync/unlinkSync, http.get/request/createServer, child_process.exec/spawn) are entirely MISSING — not even in external_potential. On the frozen substrate the sole real JS file (service-worker.js, full of caches.open()/fetch()/cache.put()) emits only 3 event-subscriber 'uses' edges and ZERO calls/imports/instantiates/function nodes, while TypeScript in the SAME package with the SAME constructs emits 25 nodes + 40 calls + 27 imports — a decisive same-package asymmetry isolating the gap to the JS (.js) analyzer specifically. The INV-javam unsupported-language guard does NOT fire because the catalog DOES exist (is_supported=True). Consequence: io-boundaries gives a SILENT clean bill of health on a Node service — fs.writeFileSync/child_process.exec/http.get all report zero I/O, output identical to a genuinely I/O-free file. Distinct from INV-judod (JS import-edge src wiring, fixed PR #3852) and WI-banaf/WI-vurop (which added unresolved-call edges for namespace/default member calls on TS but the .js path emits nothing at all). Fix surface: JS analyzer body-call/import/function-node emission (likely a .js-vs-.ts dispatch gap). filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31)."  # f3e3
    fields: {}  # f3e3
- op: discuss  # f4a4
  at: '2026-06-07T06:42:50Z'  # f4a4
  by: agent  # f4a4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f4a4
  clock: 2  # f4a4
  nonce: f4a4  # f4a4
  message: "Dogfood enrichment (member F159.A2-c) — websocket-linker src-anchor facet, reproduces on the frozen substrate. The websocket-linker's WS calls edges use a file:file anchor as src (typescript:packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts:1-1:file:file — a FILE node, not a call site) because the TS client symbol is never extracted as a real symbol. This is the SYMBOL-extraction side of this row (JS/TS analyzer emits zero real body-call/symbol nodes): with no TS call-site symbol available, the linker falls back to the file anchor as the edge src. So the WS cross-language edges are file-anchored rather than symbol-anchored as a downstream consequence of the missing TS symbol extraction this row tracks. Cross-ref WI-zurig (the WS phantom-from-test-fixture edges that ride on this file anchor) and U20/WI-fizir (server_framework dep-blind on the same edges)."  # f4a4
